  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "In the reaction of oxalate with permanganate in acidic medium, the number of electrons involved in producing one molecule of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "dr87R",
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YW5vQ",
      "text": "<math><mn>10</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "A7Pm6",
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OFF6b",
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> goes from <math><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> oxidation state to <math><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math> oxidation state.<br /><br />Total <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;transferred for <math><mn>10</mn></math> molecules of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.<br /><br />Hence, for <math><mn>1</mn></math> molecule of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, only one <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math> is transferred.<br />So, number&nbsp;of electrons involved for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> molecule of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp; is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.<br />&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
